50 706 Td (Summary) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 692 Td (This study evaluated the quality of the MediHelp system using the ISO/IEC 25010 Software) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 678 Td (Quality Model, focusing on Functional Suitability, Reliability, Usability, Performance) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 664 Td (Efficiency, Compatibility, Security, Maintainability, and Portability. Data were collected) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 650 Td (from 62 respondents through a structured survey questionnaire.) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 636 Td (The central tendency of each category, measured using the mean, showed consistently high) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 622 Td (ratings: Functionality \(4.5465\), Reliability \(4.4918\), Usability \(4.5519\), Performance) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 608 Td (Efficiency \(4.5465\), Compatibility \(4.5246\), Security \(4.5639\), Maintainability \(4.5485\),) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 594 Td (and Portability \(4.541\). All values fall within the "Excellent" interpretation range.) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 580 Td (In terms of distribution shape, all categories exhibited approximately symmetrical) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 566 Td (distributions, as indicated by the closeness of the mean and median values. This suggests) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 552 Td (that the responses are evenly distributed and not skewed.) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 538 Td (The variability of responses was low across all categories, supported by small standard) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 524 Td (deviation values and the absence of outliers. This indicates a high level of consistency) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 510 Td (among respondents' evaluations.) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 496 Td (Among the evaluated characteristics, Security \(mean = 4.5639\) obtained the highest central) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 482 Td (tendency, making it the strongest feature of the system. Conversely, Reliability \(mean =) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 468 Td (4.4918\) obtained the lowest central tendency, making it the least rated characteristic,) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 454 Td (although it still falls under the "Excellent" category.) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 440 Td (Conclusion) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 426 Td (Based on the statistical results, the MediHelp system meets the quality standards defined by) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 412 Td (the ISO/IEC 25010 model. All evaluated characteristics achieved high mean scores, indicating) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 398 Td (strong user satisfaction across all dimensions of system quality.) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 384 Td (The symmetrical distribution of responses and low variability further confirm that user) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 370 Td (evaluations are consistent and reliable. Additionally, hypothesis testing results show that) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 356 Td (most categories do not significantly differ from the benchmark mean of 4.5, reinforcing that) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 342 Td (the system is highly acceptable. Only usability showed a statistically significant) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 328 Td (difference, indicating it performs even better than the expected standard.) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 314 Td (Given these findings, it can be concluded that the MediHelp system demonstrates a high level) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 300 Td (of quality, reliability, and user acceptance. Therefore, the system is ready for deployment) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 286 Td (and has effectively passed user evaluation.) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 272 Td (Recommendation) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 258 Td (Although all categories were rated as "Excellent," improvements should be directed toward) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 244 Td (the relatively lower-performing characteristics to further enhance system quality.) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 230 Td (The following recommendations are proposed:) Tj
-50 -14 Td
50 216 Td (Improve Reliability \(Lowest Mean: 4.4918\)) Tj
-50 -14 Td
